@startuml suffix-graph-publish
' ============================================================================
' Persistent suffix-graph write — "rebuild a candidate off to the side, log the
' operation segment durably, then publish by pointer-identity CAS".
' Concurrent readers keep traversing the OLD immutable snapshot until the swap.
'
' Source of truth: src/persistent_artrie/suffix_automaton.rs
'   (mutate_retryable — Prepare → CoW clone → apply_op →
'    ArcSwap::compare_and_swap (Arc::ptr_eq) → Commit; MAX_CAS_RETRIES = 64).
'   One implementation PER FAMILY, same protocol: NativeSuffixIndex (suffix_automaton.rs),
'   NativeSuffixTreeIndex (suffix_tree.rs), NativeScdawgIndex (scdawg.rs).
'
' Color key:  green  #C8E6C9 = in-memory immutable graph snapshot (reader-visible)
'             orange #FFCC80 = durable on-disk operation-segment WAL (append + fsync)
'             amber  #FFE0B2 = control / linearization (the pointer-identity CAS)
'             grey   #ECEFF1 = note / infrastructure
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 110
skinparam maxMessageSize 100
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #37474F
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #F9A825
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
skinparam noteBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam participantBorderColor #37474F

title Persistent suffix graph — CoW rebuild, log, then CAS-publish\n(reads never block; acknowledged ⟹ durable AND visible)

actor "Writer" as WR
actor "Reader\n(concurrent)" as RD
participant "Old snapshot\n(immutable)" as OLD #C8E6C9
participant "Candidate\n(rebuilt)" as NEW #C8E6C9
participant "WAL\n(op-seg)" as WAL #FFCC80
participant "ArcSwap\n(linearize)" as ROOT #FFE0B2

note over OLD, ROOT #ECEFF1 : `ArcSwap` holds the current root. Readers `load_full()`\nan immutable `Arc` snapshot and traverse it lock-free.

== Concurrent reads observe the committed snapshot — no writer lock ==
RD -> ROOT : load_full()
activate ROOT
ROOT --> RD : Arc(old snapshot)
deactivate ROOT
RD -> OLD : match_positions(q)\n/ contains(q)
activate OLD
OLD --> RD : results (OLD graph)
deactivate OLD

== Step 1 — durability gate: append Prepare DURABLE, before any visibility ==
WR -> WAL : append Prepare\n{op_id, op} (fsync)
activate WAL
WAL --> WR : Lsn — Prepare **durable**
deactivate WAL
note right of WR #ECEFF1 : op_id = fetch_add(1).\nLog-before-publish:\nnever visible before\nits op is durable.

== Step 2 — rebuild the candidate off to the side (copy-on-write) ==
WR -> OLD : clone snapshot
activate OLD
OLD --> NEW : deep copy
deactivate OLD
WR -> NEW : apply_op(op)\n(insert / remove /\nset_value / compact)
activate NEW
NEW --> WR : candidate ready
deactivate NEW
note over OLD, NEW #ECEFF1 : Readers still see the **old snapshot** —\nthe candidate is private until the CAS.

== Step 3 — publish: pointer-identity CAS (the linearization point) ==
loop until the root CAS wins (≤ MAX_CAS_RETRIES = 64)
  WR -> ROOT : compare_and_swap\n(old, Arc(new))
  activate ROOT
  alt Arc::ptr_eq(previous, old) — WIN
    ROOT --> WR : published — NEW is live
    deactivate ROOT
  else lost a race
    ROOT --> WR : retry: reload +\nrebuild on newer base
  end
end

== Step 4 — commit marker, then acknowledge ==
WR -> WAL : append Commit\n{op_id} (fsync)
activate WAL
WAL --> WR : Lsn — committed_op_id\n.fetch_max(op_id)
deactivate WAL
WR -> WR : Ack — **durable AND visible**

note over OLD #ECEFF1 : Old snapshot is reclaimed once the last\nreader holding its `Arc` drops it (no reader interrupted).

note across #FFF9C4 : **Crash semantics.** On reopen the checkpoint image loads, then the durable WAL\ntail replays: Prepares with a durable Commit apply in op_id order; un-committed Prepares are\ndropped. Recovery also folds the historical length-prefixed monolithic WAL format when present.
@enduml
